# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build — an allowlist.
#
# It used to be a denylist (node_modules/, .env, scripts/ …), and a denylist
# only covers the files someone thought of: backend/.scratch-family.json, the
# shared fixture's working password, sat beside it and went up with every
# source deploy (29 Sep 2026 review, finding 17). So now nothing goes unless
# it is named here, and what is named is exactly what the Dockerfile COPYs:
#   package.json, package-lock.json  (npm ci, both stages)
#   tsconfig.json, src/, build/      (npm run build, first stage)
# A new COPY in the Dockerfile needs a line here and in .dockerignore, or the
# build fails on a missing file — loudly, which is the direction to fail in.
#
# When a .gcloudignore exists gcloud does not read .gitignore, so this file is
# the whole rule. Check it with: gcloud meta list-files-for-upload

/*
!/Dockerfile
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/tsconfig.json
!/src/
!/build/

# Inside what is let in: the tests (fixtures, mocks, staging credentials'
# names) and the notes never reach the image.
/src/__tests__/
/src/**/*.md
